Z||000005||mbramble||11-23-2001||08:31 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adrift:<BR><B>...which don't really belong in Tech. Discussion or General....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If they are based on Fieros then they certainly belong here.  Much more than a big chunk of the garbage that gets posted in Tech and General that has <B>nothing</B> at all to do with Fieros.  Besides, it would not matter if 5 more Forums were started, many people have not a clue when and where to post threads so your kit car forum would have the same old junk that shows up here but should be in the O/T section.<P><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||beer_stud_21||11-23-2001||09:24 PM||||I broached the subject of breaking up the catagories into "sub sections" but the idea didn't go over to well.  The idea basically got shot down like it was the afgani air force...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">  Personally I think its a good idea.  But aparently not many others do.  <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010038.html" TARGET=_blank>Here's what I'm talkin about.</A><P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||11-23-2001||09:50 PM||||I was planning to open a "purely mods" forum on my site.. mostly for fieros, but I'd love to include mods for other cars as well. Jaei Sun used to have an article on his website about a custom air intake on his Beretta... that's the kind of stuff I'm talking about.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm by no means trying to break up the forum, just saying there has been some interest in a mods forum, but not much interest in having a separate one here.. so I figured I could make a forum of my own, JUST FOR MODS... no general tech questions, etc.. no way would I ever do anything that looked like I was trying to replace PFF...<P>Sections would be:<BR>-kit cars<BR>-interior & exterior modifications<BR>-engine modifications<BR>-stereos<P>what do you think??<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000008||artherd||11-23-2001||10:20 PM||||How does *any* of this not fit into Tech?<P>Everything proposed as a 'seperate' area already has a seperate area! If it's at all technical, and has *something* to do with Fieros *somewhere* down the line, then it belongs in Tech!<P>I've see too many forums *segregate* untill you're fricking blind and confused and people leave, then the fourm dies. It's that simple.<P>Cliff has managed to keep the fourm wonderfly simple and navigable, while dealing with an ever increasing volume effectively and smoothly.  Pennock's is probally the most active and helpful fourm I've ever been on.<P>It's like an 'open plan' studio, it encourages collaboration, and we all work together and are exposed to things we may not have planned on being exposed too.<P>We're *greater* than the sum of our parts this way.<P>I say, Keep It Simple, Cliffy!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||Adrift||11-30-2001||09:20 PM||||I dunno... I just thought it would be nice to have a place to ask specific fiero-based kit cars builders questions. The truth is less then 1% of this board are building kit cars, and if I ask a question specific to kit car building there is a very good chance that it will get knocked down to msg #110 before any of the other builders even get to read it... and I would feel bad constantly bumping it up to the top, that would just get annoying :P<P>Maybe I'll just start a kit car forum seperate from pennocks, I guess that will solve my problem :P||||reg||1
